Let's write a GraphQL query. Linear's GraphQL API (publicly documented):

```graphql
{
  teams {
    nodes {
      id
      name
      key
      workflowStates(first: 50) {
        nodes {
          id
          name
          type
        }
      }
    }
  }
  users(filter: {name: {contains: "Priya Nair"}}) {
    nodes {
      id
      name
      email
    }
  }
}
```

Then issues:

```graphql
{
  issues(filter: {
    team: {key: {eq: "WEB"}},
    state: {type: {eq: "completed"}},
    assignee: {id: {eq: "..."}},
    completedAt: {eq: "2026-10-02T00:00:00Z"}  # probably need a date filter
  }) {
    nodes {
      id
      identifier
      title
      description
      priority
      completedAt
      assignee { name }
      state { name }
    }
  }
}
```

Actually, the issue filter supports `completedAt` as a date filter (DateOperator: eq, neq, lt, lte, gt, gte). Let's try it.

The priority update mutation: `issueUpdate(input: {id: "...", priority: 4})` — in Linear, priority is 0 (none), 1 (low), 2 (medium), 3 (high), 4 (urgent).

